What is an Object?
An object is a thing that has:
    Attributes (data) — what it has.
    Methods (behavior) — what it can do.

A class is a template for creating objects. One class can create many objects.

The Constructor: __init__
A constructor runs automatically whenever an object is created. The constructor initializes the object.

The self Keyword - self refers to the current object. You do not pass self yourself.
Adding Methods - Methods are functions inside a class.
Instance Variables - Variables stored inside self belong to each object.

